repository-code: "https://github.com/web3guru888/agentverse-2030-paper"
abstract: >
  This paper presents a systematic analysis of Agentverse, the agent cloud
  platform developed by Fetch.ai and operated by the Artificial Superintelligence
  (ASI) Alliance, as a case study in agent-native infrastructure. We contribute:
  (1) a Gap Taxonomy of 52 missing capabilities across 8 categories derived from
  an empirical audit of 204 API endpoints; (2) a seven-layer Agent Cloud Stack
  reference architecture for 2030; and (3) five critical evolution paths from the
  current platform to a fully realised agent cloud.
